{"name":"Queens of the Dead","hex":"#652793","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"queens","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of queen"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pair of queens."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/queens"},{"term":"dead","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["No longer living; deceased.","Devoid of living things; barren."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Exactly.","Very, absolutely, extremely."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dead"}],"entries":[{"title":"Queens of the Dead","blocks":[{"text":"Queens of the Dead is a 2025 American zombie comedy film written and directed by Tina Romero. It stars Katy O'Brian, Jaquel Spivey, Riki Lindhome, Jack Haven, Cheyenne Jackson, and Margaret Cho."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/de/Queens_of_the_Dead_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Queens_of_the_Dead"},{"title":"Queens","blocks":[{"text":"Queens is the largest by area of the five boroughs of New York City, and the second most populous, with a population of 2,405,464 as of the 2020 census. Since 1899 the borough is coextensive with Queens County, the second-most populous county in New York state, behind Kings County (Brooklyn). If Queens were its own city, it would be the fourth most-populous in the United States, after the other four boroughs of New York City, Los Angeles, and Chicago. Queens is the fourth-most densely populated borough in New York City and the fourth-most densely populated U.S. county."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Flushing_Meadows_May_2024_64.jpg/330px-Flushing_Meadows_May_2024_64.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Queens"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/de/Queens_of_the_Dead_poster.jpg